  "goodToKnow": "Der Flugplatz is an airfield, usually smaller than a Flughafen (airport): ein Segelflugplatz (gliding field), ein Militärflugplatz. Berlin's Tempelhof airport, famous for the 1948–49 airlift (Luftbrücke), closed in 2008 and became the Tempelhofer Feld, a huge public park; in a 2014 referendum, Berliners voted against building on it. Plural: die Flugplätze."
